From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: give every sample an explicit size

Create each compressed sample handed to VideoToolbox with a one-entry
sample size array holding the whole bitstream length, where the hwaccel
used to pass no size array at all. VideoToolbox's Dolby Vision HEVC
decoder fails samples without it with kCMBlockBufferBadLengthParameterErr.
The change applies to every codec the hwaccel decodes (H.264, HEVC, AV1,
VP9, MPEG and ProRes); each sample still holds exactly one frame.

Part of Lucid Engine's Dolby Vision support. Applies to FFmpeg n8.0.1 on
top of Vivid's patches 0001 and 0002.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for
FFmpeg. Like the file it modifies, it is free software; you can
